4 main job profiles

Why 4 main job profiles?

The answer is hidden in the previous days. We learnt about MDLC.
MDLC is large. It has 9 steps. One person cannot do all steps alone.

1. Data Engineer

A data engineer brings all the data for making ML models.

In big companies they use OLTP (online transaction processing).
Example: Flipkart. From OLTP we get OLAP (online analytical processing).
OLTP holds the actual running data in the database. OLAP is for analysis. OLAP can be called a data warehouse. OLTP can be called the database.

Data engineer tasks:
Scrape data from given sources
Move and store data in OLAP, secure servers, or warehouse
Build data pipelines and APIs for easy access to data
Handle database and data warehouse

This is the most important job role when we have a large scale of data.
Data is gold.

Skills for data engineer:
Software development, database, data structures and algorithms
Programming languages, RDBMS, big data tools
Cloud platforms like AWS and GCP
Distributed systems and data pipelines

It is very difficult. It is hardcore software work.

2. Data Analyst

In MDLC, the first steps like data gathering are done with help from the data engineer.
Then the analyst cleans and organizes the data.
Summarize past data. Example: why did a particular product fail in the business?
Create data visualization
Produce and maintain reports
Collaborate with teams and colleagues based on insight
Optimize data collection procedures

Data analyst and business analyst are almost similar. Just the tools are different.

Skills:
Statistical programming and programming languages
Creative and analytical thinking
Strong communication skills
Data mining and cleaning
Data visualization and data storytelling
SQL
Advanced Microsoft Excel
Domain skills for the field you work in. Example: if you work in medical field, know the medical domain.

3. Data Scientist

A person who is better at statistics than any software engineer, and better at software engineering than any statistician.

The data scientist can do almost every work in MDLC.

The data analyst looks at the past.
The data scientist works for the future.
Works on recommendations from point A to point B.
The data analyst gives a summary.

The ultimate goal should be to become a data scientist.
It is also called ML fullstack.

We need communication skills as well.
Very good at maths.

4. ML Engineer

Once the model is ready, the ML engineer deploys it.
Scaling and optimizing the model for production.
Does monitoring and optimization of the model.

Skills:
Mathematics, programming language, distributed systems
Data, model, and evaluation
Software engineering and system design

Comparing all of these:

Data Analyst: Analytical HIGH, Business MEDIUM TO HIGH, Data Storytelling HIGH, Soft Skills MEDIUM TO HIGH, Software MEDIUM
Data Engineer: Analytical MEDIUM, Business LOW, Data Storytelling LOW, Soft Skills MEDIUM, Software HIGH
Data Scientist: Analytical HIGH, Business HIGH, Data Storytelling HIGH, Soft Skills HIGH, Software MEDIUM
ML Engineer: Analytical MEDIUM TO HIGH, Business MEDIUM, Data Storytelling LOW, Soft Skills HIGH, Software HIGH
